---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="hero-name">L. June Bloch</h1>
      <p class="hero-identity">Anthropologist · Ethnic Studies · Builder</p>
      <p class="hero-intro">
        I write about how systems produce violence, and I build small tools that try
        to interrupt some of it at the layer I can actually reach. Reframe structures
        LLM prompts to route through critical-theory frameworks before responding.
        Autograder reads student work with a local LLM and surfaces patterns for the
        teacher. The publications develop the theory; the software experiments with
        what happens when you try to put pieces of it into prompt-time scaffolding.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-practice">
        I bring the same practice across scholarship, software, and consulting: studying how
        institutions and technologies make some knowledge legible and push other knowledge toward
        the margins, then building to see what a different architecture makes possible.
        <a href="/consulting/">Explore consulting</a>
      </p>
      <div class="hero-socials">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=9bQ8kjIAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao" aria-label="Google Scholar">Scholar</a>
        <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/disabledbydesign.bsky.social" aria-label="Bluesky">Bluesky</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/disabledbydesign" aria-label="GitHub">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/l-june-bloch-1897a329/" aria-label="LinkedIn">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="mailto:june@ljunebloch.com" aria-label="Email">june@ljunebloch.com</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-image">
      <img
        src="/images/headshot-branded.png"
        alt="Dr. L. June Bloch"
        width="280"
        height="350"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <a href="/research/" class="feature-link">
        <h2>Research</h2>
        <p>An elder said: "Did you ever consider that it isn't a bird?" It was a moth. That question reorganized fifteen years of fieldwork and five research programs.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/publications/" class="feature-link">
        <h2>Publications</h2>
        <p><em>Cultural Anthropology</em>, <em>American Anthropologist</em>, <em>Current Anthropology</em> — recognition, animacy, settler colonialism, genocide, algorithmic justice, Indigenous knowledge, trans studies, and the politics of care.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/projects/" class="feature-link">
        <h2>Software</h2>
        <p>"There is no neutral condition; bias surfaces in qualitatively different ways across contexts." Open-source tools I built from teaching conditions and the critical-theory questions running through the research — Reframe, Autograder, EvalEye, RoboStripper, and more.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/teaching/" class="feature-link">
        <h2>Teaching</h2>
        <p>Ethnic Studies was created by student strikes. The pedagogy should honor that — consensus-based, horizontal, survivable. No late penalties, reading equivalencies, emergency flex weeks.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>


</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-practice {
    max-width: 43rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--amber-dim);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .hero-practice a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
